# Rank 1364 / CVE-2022-39252 (GHSA-vp68-2wrm-69qm, RUSTSEC-2022-0085, CWE-287):
# matrix-sdk-crypto accepted an `m.forwarded_room_key` from whichever device the
# homeserver chose to deliver it from, as long as the key answered some room-key
# request the client had made. A malicious homeserver could therefore inject
# megolm session keys of its own into the store and have later events in the room
# attributed to whoever the injected session claimed, which is impersonation.
#
# GossipMachine::receive_supported_keys in
# crates/matrix-sdk-crypto/src/gossiping/machine.rs made exactly one check before
# committing the key: `if let Some(info) = self.get_key_info(event).await?`, which
# is `Store::get_secret_request_by_info` -- did we ask for a key with this room
# id, session id and algorithm. It matched the request record, not the responder.
# `info.request_recipient`, the device the request is actually sent to, is never
# read, and the Olm envelope's own Curve25519 identity key -- the only field that
# identifies the sender, as opposed to `content.claimed_sender_key`, which the
# sender writes itself -- passes straight through to
# accept_forwarded_room_key as the identity to store the session under. The same
# file does this correctly one protocol path over: receive_secret resolves
# the envelope key with `self.store.get_device_from_curve_key(&event.sender,
# sender_key)` and requires `device.user_id() == self.user_id() &&
# device.is_verified()` before accepting an `m.secret.send`. The forwarded
# room-key path had no equivalent.
#
# Corpus correction. The pool named 41449d2cc360e347f5d4e1c154ec1e3185f11acd,
# which is `test(crypto): Test that we reject forwarded room keys from other
# users` -- 60 added lines, all of them a `#[async_test]` in the same file. The
# advisory references two commits and the fixing one is the other, its parent
# 093fb5d0aa21c0b5eaea6ec96b477f1075271cbb, `fix(crypto): Only accept forwarded
# room keys from our own trusted devices`. That commit adds
# GossipMachine::should_accept_forward, which performs the lookup receive_secret
# performed, and wraps the acceptance in it:
#
#   if self.should_accept_forward(&info, sender_key).await? {
#       self.accept_forwarded_room_key(&info, &event.sender, sender_key, algorithm, content).await
#   } else { warn!(..); Ok(None) }
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap: no cross-procedural view of a neutralising control in
# Rust. The concept is not the problem -- code.ProtocolStateReview (VYQL-AUTH-082,
# CWE_287 among its five) covers unauthenticated protocol data accepted without
# the state check that is supposed to gate it, and a Kotlin binding for this
# exact weakness in another Matrix SDK emits it. The problem is that the
# fix is a delegation: inside receive_supported_keys, the entire local footprint
# of the change is one call to a newly added private method. Every fact the Rust
# frontend offers about a function is confined to that function's own body --
# rsFunctionContext in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/rust.go emits one
# `analysis.function.context` node per function whose `call_path:`, `call_arg:`
# and `selector:` tokens come from walking that body, and Rust emits no
# `analysis.class.context` node for an `impl` block at all -- so the store lookup
# and verification state that now gate the acceptance are, to a binding, simply
# absent from the function that accepts.
#
# Measured. A function-scoped binding for the shape runs against
# both revisions of the real repository with
# `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB -flags only`:
#
#   node.scope == "function"
#   and containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["accept_forwarded_room_key", "from_forwarded_key"])
#   and not (containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["get_device_from_curve_key", "is_verified", "get_device"]))
#
# It reports two flags at 093fb5d0^ -- machine.rs:950, receive_supported_keys,
# the vulnerable function, and machine.rs:874, accept_forwarded_room_key -- and
# two flags at 093fb5d0, the same two functions at 874 and 965. Identical output
# on the vulnerable and the fixed revision: no discrimination whatever. Adding
# `should_accept_forward` to the negation drops the fixed revision to one flag,
# which is what the absence of any generic fact costs -- the only thing that
# separates the two revisions inside the accepting function is one crate-private
# method name, and a binding naming it recognises this patch rather than the
# weakness. machine.rs:874 also stays flagged on both revisions either way,
# because accept_forwarded_room_key is where `InboundGroupSession::from_forwarded_key`
# is called -- the documented API that turns a forwarded payload into a stored
# session, and therefore the only anchor for this shape derivable from
# matrix-sdk-crypto's documentation -- and the fixed revision does not touch that function;
# it is the caller that had to authenticate.
#
# The minimal pair below isolates the construct. Both fixed forms perform the
# same two lookups on the same two values and reach the same acceptance call; they
# differ only in whether the lookups sit in the accepting function or one call
# away in a sibling `impl` method. The inline one is discriminated correctly, the
# delegated one is not, and the delegated one is what the fixed revision ships.
# Widening the neutralising scope from the function to the `impl` block or the
# file is measured wrong rather than merely coarse: machine.rs's own receive_secret
# performs `get_device_from_curve_key` and `is_verified` for `m.secret.send` in
# the same `impl` as the vulnerable function, so a scope that reaches it suppresses
# the true positive. The fourth case pins that -- an authenticated sibling path for
# a different protocol message does not authenticate this one.
#
# Behaviour a shippable fact needs: the structured context tokens of an
# intra-file resolved callee attributed to the caller's function context, one hop
# and bounded, so a check factored into a helper reads as present in the function
# that calls it. `vyql resolve` over the fixed form reports
# `self.should_accept_forward` unresolved, so the hop is not available from call
# resolution either.
#
# No definition change attempted. Nothing is reported for any of the four forms
# today, and the cases pin that.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, all four forms rejected.

test "rank1364: a forwarded room key is accepted on a request match alone, with no check on the sending device"
  lang rust
  file crates/matrix-sdk-crypto/src/gossiping/machine.rs
  reject_review code.ProtocolStateReview
  code
  ```
  impl GossipMachine {
      async fn accept_forwarded_room_key(
          &self,
          info: &GossipRequest,
          sender: &UserId,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
          algorithm: EventEncryptionAlgorithm,
          content: &ForwardedMegolmV1AesSha2Content,
      ) -> Result<Option<InboundGroupSession>, CryptoStoreError> {
          match InboundGroupSession::from_forwarded_key(&algorithm, content) {
              Ok(session) => {
                  let old_session = self
                      .store
                      .get_inbound_group_session(
                          session.room_id(),
                          &session.sender_key.to_base64(),
                          session.session_id(),
                      )
                      .await?;

                  let session = if let Some(old_session) = old_session {
                      if session.compare(&old_session).await == SessionOrdering::Better {
                          self.mark_as_done(info).await?;
                          Some(session)
                      } else {
                          None
                      }
                  } else {
                      self.mark_as_done(info).await?;
                      Some(session)
                  };

                  Ok(session)
              }
              Err(e) => {
                  warn!(
                      %sender,
                      sender_key = sender_key.to_base64(),
                      claimed_sender_key = content.claimed_sender_key.to_base64(),
                      "Couldn't create a group session from a received room key"
                  );
                  Err(e.into())
              }
          }
      }

      /// Receive a forwarded room key event that was sent using any of our
      /// supported content types.
      async fn receive_supported_keys(
          &self,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
          event: &DecryptedForwardedRoomKeyEvent,
          content: &ForwardedMegolmV1AesSha2Content,
      ) -> Result<Option<InboundGroupSession>, CryptoStoreError> {
          let algorithm = event.content.algorithm();

          if let Some(info) = self.get_key_info(event).await? {
              self.accept_forwarded_room_key(&info, &event.sender, sender_key, algorithm, content)
                  .await
          } else {
              warn!(
                  sender = %event.sender,
                  sender_key = %sender_key,
                  room_id = %content.room_id,
                  session_id = content.session_id.as_str(),
                  claimed_sender_key = %content.claimed_sender_key,
                  algorithm = %algorithm,
                  "Received a forwarded room key that we didn't request",
              );

              Ok(None)
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1364: acceptance gated by a sender-device check factored into a sibling impl method"
  lang rust
  file crates/matrix-sdk-crypto/src/gossiping/machine.rs
  reject_review code.ProtocolStateReview
  code
  ```
  impl GossipMachine {
      async fn should_accept_forward(
          &self,
          info: &GossipRequest,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
      ) -> Result<bool, CryptoStoreError> {
          let device =
              self.store.get_device_from_curve_key(&info.request_recipient, sender_key).await?;

          if let Some(device) = device {
              Ok(device.user_id() == self.user_id() && device.is_verified())
          } else {
              Ok(false)
          }
      }

      /// Receive a forwarded room key event that was sent using any of our
      /// supported content types.
      async fn receive_supported_keys(
          &self,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
          event: &DecryptedForwardedRoomKeyEvent,
          content: &ForwardedMegolmV1AesSha2Content,
      ) -> Result<Option<InboundGroupSession>, CryptoStoreError> {
          let algorithm = event.content.algorithm();

          if let Some(info) = self.get_key_info(event).await? {
              if self.should_accept_forward(&info, sender_key).await? {
                  self.accept_forwarded_room_key(&info, &event.sender, sender_key, algorithm, content)
                      .await
              } else {
                  warn!(
                      sender = %event.sender,
                      %sender_key,
                      room_id = %content.room_id,
                      session_id = content.session_id.as_str(),
                      claimed_sender_key = %content.claimed_sender_key,
                      "Received a forwarded room key from an unknown device, or \
                       from a device that the key request recipient doesn't own",
                  );

                  Ok(None)
              }
          } else {
              warn!(
                  sender = %event.sender,
                  sender_key = %sender_key,
                  room_id = %content.room_id,
                  session_id = content.session_id.as_str(),
                  claimed_sender_key = %content.claimed_sender_key,
                  algorithm = %algorithm,
                  "Received a forwarded room key that we didn't request",
              );

              Ok(None)
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1364: the same sender-device check performed inline in the accepting function"
  lang rust
  file crates/matrix-sdk-crypto/src/gossiping/machine.rs
  reject_review code.ProtocolStateReview
  code
  ```
  impl GossipMachine {
      /// Receive a forwarded room key event that was sent using any of our
      /// supported content types.
      async fn receive_supported_keys(
          &self,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
          event: &DecryptedForwardedRoomKeyEvent,
          content: &ForwardedMegolmV1AesSha2Content,
      ) -> Result<Option<InboundGroupSession>, CryptoStoreError> {
          let algorithm = event.content.algorithm();

          if let Some(info) = self.get_key_info(event).await? {
              let device =
                  self.store.get_device_from_curve_key(&info.request_recipient, sender_key).await?;

              if let Some(device) = device {
                  if device.user_id() == self.user_id() && device.is_verified() {
                      return self
                          .accept_forwarded_room_key(
                              &info,
                              &event.sender,
                              sender_key,
                              algorithm,
                              content,
                          )
                          .await;
                  }
              }

              warn!(
                  sender = %event.sender,
                  %sender_key,
                  room_id = %content.room_id,
                  "Received a forwarded room key from an unknown device, or \
                   from a device that the key request recipient doesn't own",
              );

              Ok(None)
          } else {
              Ok(None)
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1364: a sibling protocol path authenticates its own sender and the forwarded-key path still does not"
  lang rust
  file crates/matrix-sdk-crypto/src/gossiping/machine.rs
  reject_review code.ProtocolStateReview
  code
  ```
  impl GossipMachine {
      async fn receive_secret(
          &self,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
          event: &DecryptedSecretSendEvent,
          request: &GossipRequest,
          secret_name: &SecretName,
      ) -> Result<(), CryptoStoreError> {
          if let Some(device) =
              self.store.get_device_from_curve_key(&event.sender, sender_key).await?
          {
              // Only accept secrets from one of our own trusted devices.
              if device.user_id() == self.user_id() && device.is_verified() {
                  self.accept_secret(event, request, secret_name).await?;
              } else {
                  warn!(
                      sender = event.sender.as_str(),
                      secret_name = secret_name.as_ref(),
                      "Received a m.secret.send event from another user or from \
                      unverified device"
                  );
              }
          }

          Ok(())
      }

      /// Receive a forwarded room key event that was sent using any of our
      /// supported content types.
      async fn receive_supported_keys(
          &self,
          sender_key: Curve25519PublicKey,
          event: &DecryptedForwardedRoomKeyEvent,
          content: &ForwardedMegolmV1AesSha2Content,
      ) -> Result<Option<InboundGroupSession>, CryptoStoreError> {
          let algorithm = event.content.algorithm();

          if let Some(info) = self.get_key_info(event).await? {
              self.accept_forwarded_room_key(&info, &event.sender, sender_key, algorithm, content)
                  .await
          } else {
              Ok(None)
          }
      }
  }
  ```
